{"id":100242045510553,"type":"album","name":"Those Once Loyal","artist":"Bolt Thrower","year":2005,"weight":12,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/59799-those-once-loyal.jpg","aoty":70,"aoty_user":85,"sputnik":4.18,"yt":"qFmE9cvHECc","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/bolt-thrower/those-once-loyal","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/59799-bolt-thrower-those-once-loyal.php","sputnikmusic":"https://www.sputnikmusic.com/album/11862/Bolt-Thrower-Those-Once-Loyal/"},"desc":"\"Those Once Loyal\" is the eighth and final studio album by British death metal band Bolt Thrower, released on 11 November 2005 by Metal Blade Records. It was recorded with producer Andy Faulkner at Sable Rose Studios in Coventry, England. The album marked the return of vocalist Karl Willetts, who rejoined the band in November 2004, making it the first Bolt Thrower release to feature him since \"Mercenary\" (1998). Musically, \"Those Once Loyal\" continues Bolt Thrower’s melodic, groove-based death metal style, with comparatively tighter song structures and arrangements and a more refined production than some of the band’s earlier releases. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":108059906834811,"name":"Bolt Thrower","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Boltthrower_foto.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":255263121494129,"type":"genre","name":"Metal","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":3474,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2333,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":62217299479553,"type":"genre","name":"Death Metal","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":311,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":251396937181996,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Death Metal","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":10,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":72396664188223,"name":"Sputnikmusic Best Albums 2005","src":"charts","